Subject: How can I add spatial correlation to designed matrix (Z) model?
Message-ID: <mYG2vZ5_ZTU.WLLrHND6BgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/mYG2vZ5_ZTU/m/WLLrHND6BgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello everyone!

I have a model that requires to add spatial correlation to Z model (designed matrix model).

In other words, I have a model y=iid_X + Zu, where Z is a designed matrix. I need to make u not a just a vector of random effects, but also spatially correlated.

I have read a few documents and but couldn't find a direct answer. I really appreciate if someone could advise on this problem.

Thanks!

From u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com  Wed Jan  6 18:50:58 2021
From: u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com (Helpdesk)
Date: Wed, 06 Jan 2021 18:50:58 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] How can I add spatial correlation to designed matrix (Z) model?
Message-ID: <mYG2vZ5_ZTU.H9z3myf7BgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <mYG2vZ5_ZTU.WLLrHND6BgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <mYG2vZ5_ZTU.WLLrHND6BgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/mYG2vZ5_ZTU/m/H9z3myf7BgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Normally the f() notation and variants is sufficient, and the Zu is just
to quickly map back to a standard/classical model, not the other way
around.

You may look at the SPDE book at www.r-inla.org <http://www.r-inla.org>  and check if you find
something there.

H

