Just to add, this is a problem with the meshbuilder as well some times.

I use pkill inla, pkill inla.mkl, etc. in the terminal. Note that you sometimes have to do it several times before the kill signal works. If you are using RStudio on a mac, I recommend using pkill _instead_ of trying to stop the process from within RStudio (as R often crashes). The pkill will cause inla/meshbuilder to fail, but your RStudio will be happy (just send you an error message).

Best, Haakon

